{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Look to Him</b> — the reason He then mentions <b>the poor man called</b> [Ps. 34:7], and its parallel is <b>I see Him, but not now</b> [Numbers 24:17], and it [refers to] a star from Jacob." "<b>and they shall be radiant</b> — their faces shall shine, opposite to <b>they shall be ashamed</b>. From the root of the word for canals, and in the Targum: <b>and their light is upon them</b>." "And some say: from the root of <b>and they shall be radiant to Him</b> — from the root נהר."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {0 "The Hebrew טעם אליו is ambiguous; read as 'the reason for Him,' i.e., the reason the verse says 'to Him.' The verse alluded to in 'its parallel' is Numbers 24:17. Ibn Ezra's point is compressed and somewhat cryptic."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:29:28.602682271Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}